One Weird Dude wrote:
> How do I identify the place I'm in without dying or recognizing it from
> before?  It used to do that with an old version of the game (e.g.
> "Welcome back to the Gnomish Mines", etc.).

I think only two branches can be entered without you noticing it
beforehand: the Gnomish mines, and Sokoban if you previously
fell through a trap door. Sokoban lvl1 is always the same
layout, so you can't be mistaken. To recognize the mines,
check that you are not in a rectangular room. This is done
immediately if the level is lit, otherwise you must follow some
walls. If the level is a dug out bones level, you can also use
this method since room floors and dug out corridors are two
different symbols. This will not work however if the ghost former
self dug pits everywhere (this should not happen very often).

You know that you are not in the first level of the Mines if you hear
level sounds (someone complaining about shoplifters, for instance).

You can also suspect that you are in the Mines if you see lots of
gnomes and dwarves.

IIRC, the only way to enter a branch is to climb stairs or ladders,
step into a magic portal, or invoke the Eye. The main branch can
also be entered by levelporting.

